.TH INET 3  "2008-Feb-04" "Linux" "Linux Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
.B ax25_aton, ax25_aton_entry, ax25_aton_arglist,
.B ax25_ntoa, ax25_cmp, ax25_validate
\- AX25 Address manipulation routines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <netax25/ax25.h>
.PP
.BI "int ax25_aton(const char *" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
.PP
.BI "int ax25_aton_arglist(const char **" cp ", struct full_sockaddr_ax25 *" fsap ");"
.PP
.BI "int ax25_aton_entry(const char *" cp ", char *" axp ");"
.PP
.BI "char *ax25_ntoa(ax25_address *" axp ");"
.PP
.BI "int ax25_cmp(ax25_address *" ax1 ", ax25_address *" ax2 ");"
.PP
.BI "int ax25_validate(char *" axp ");"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR ax25_aton ()
takes the ASCII string
.I cp
that is in the format
.I callsign
.RI [[ V | VIA ] callsign "...]"
and stores it in
.I fsap
in network format.
.PP
.BR ax25_aton_entry ()
takes the ASCII string of a callsign
.I cp
and stores it in network format in
.I axp.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_aton_arglist ()
takes a NULL terminated array of strings
.I cp
and stores it in
.I fsap
in network format.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_ntoa ()
takes a network format address
.I axp
and returns the ASCII representation.
The string is returned in a statically allocated buffer, which
subsequent calls will overwrite.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_cmp ()
function compares the two ax25 addresses,
.I ax1
and
.IR ax2 ,
that are in network format and determines whether they are identical,
differ only by their SSIDs or are different.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_validate ()
function checks to see if the address
.I axp
in network format is a correctly formatted address.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
The
.BR ax25_aton () and
.BR ax25_aton_arglist ()
functions return -1 if an error occurs otherwise the length of
the returned structure.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_aton_entry ()
function returns -1 if an error occurs otherwise zero.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_cmp ()
function returns 0 if the two addresses are identical, 1 if they are
different or 2 is only the SSIDs are different.
.PP
The
.BR ax25_validate ()
function returns TRUE if the callsign is valid or FALSE if it is not.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ax25 "(4), " netrom "(4), " rose "(4)"

.SH "AX.25 CONFIGURATION INTERFACE"
The following functions provide access to the AX.25 port configuration
as defined in
.IR axports (5).
They are declared in
.IR <netax25/axconfig.h> .

.SS "Library Initialization"
.TP
.BI "int ax25_config_load_ports(void)"
Reads the
.I axports
file and builds the internal port table.  Must be called before
using any other configuration function.  Returns the number of
active ports, or 0 on failure.

.SS "Port Enumeration and Lookup"
.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_next(char *" name ")"
Enumerates all configured ports.  Pass NULL to get the first port name,
subsequent calls with the last returned name return the next port.
Returns NULL at end of list or on error.

.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_name(char *" device ")"
Maps a device name (kernel interface) to the corresponding port name
from
.IR axports .
Returns NULL on error.

.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_addr(char *" name ")"
Returns the callsign (in ASCII) configured for the given port name.
Returns NULL if the port is not known.

.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_dev(char *" name ")"
Returns the kernel network device name for the given port.
Only returns a device for ports served by the kernel AX.25 stack
(i.e. ports whose callsign matches an interface that is up).
Returns NULL for userspace ports (WAMPES, AGWPE) or on error.

.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_conf_dev(char *" name ")"
Returns the device name as configured in
.IR axports ,
regardless of whether the port is served by the kernel, a WAMPES
node, or an AGWPE server.  Returns NULL if the port is not known.

.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_port(ax25_address *" callsign ")"
Maps a callsign to the port name that owns it.  A null AX.25
address returns
.Q *
meaning all ports.  Returns NULL on error.

.SS "Port Parameters"
.TP
.BI "int ax25_config_get_window(char *" name ")"
Returns the default window size for the port.  Returns 0 on error.

.TP
.BI "int ax25_config_get_paclen(char *" name ")"
Returns the maximum packet length for the port.  Returns 0 on error.

.TP
.BI "int ax25_config_get_baud(char *" name ")"
Returns the baud rate for the port.  Returns 0 on error.

.TP
.BI "char *ax25_config_get_desc(char *" name ")"
Returns the description string for the port.  Returns NULL on error.

.SS "Backend and Kernel Information"
.TP
.BI "int ax25_config_port_is_kernel(const char *" name ")"
Returns non-zero if the named port is served by the kernel AX.25
stack (i.e. its callsign matches an interface that is up).

.TP
.BI "int ax25_config_kernel_ports(void)"
Returns the number of ports that are served by the kernel AX.25 stack.

.TP
.BI "int ax25_port_info(const char *" name ", struct ax25_port_info *" info ")"
Fills the
.I info
structure with all available information about the port:
backend (kernel, WAMPES, AGWPE), callsign, device, description,
window, paclen, baud, and backend-specific fields (WAMPES node name,
AGWPE flat port, channel, upstream).
Returns 0 on success, -1 on error.

.TP
.BI "int ax25_port_number(const char *" name ")"
Returns the flat AGWPE port number for the given port, or -1 with
errno set to EADDRNOTAVAIL if the port is not an AGWPE port.

.SS "File Access"
.TP
.BI "const char *ax25_config_ports_file(void)"
Returns the path to the
.I axports
file used by the library.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ax25 "(4), " netrom "(4), " rose "(4), " axports "(5)"
